    "proof": "Expand (1-e^(itheta))^m. The moment sums are m-th finite differences of polynomials of degree below m and therefore vanish exactly. The maximum of |1-e^(itheta)| is two, attained at pi. Abel multiplication contributes rho^(M+r), so the transformed binomial factors as rho^M(1-rho e^(itheta))^m/2^m. Evaluating at pi proves both the norm formula and the lower bound.",
